+## Song names on the banner (main21 patch 135)
+
+A song of your folder gets the EA GAMES TRAX banner when it starts: title, artist and album from its tags (`xst_read_tags`: ID3v2 and ID3v1 in
+mp3, Vorbis comments in flac and ogg). No title tag: the name in the list. No artist tag: the soundtrack's (folder's) name. m4a and wav tags are not read. The font shows Latin-1,
+other characters as `?`, and each text is cut at 31 characters. A mod's song keeps the texts its mod declares.
+
+## Mixing with EA GAMES TRAX (main21 patch 136)
+
+MASHUP SETTINGS > MOD SETTINGS > BURNOUT MASHUP > **MIX WITH EA TRAX** (default off; needs a music folder). While on, the next song comes from all the folder's
+songs and the 44 EA GAMES TRAX tracks, each song as likely. This is its own option, separate from the screen's random order (Y): while the mix is on the order inside each
+source is random whatever Y says; Y is not changed, and applies again with the mix off. EA GAMES TRAX tracks switched off in the screen stay off (none left: custom music only).
+The title has one source at a time, so a change of source is a stop and a start: no crossfade, and a song can come back sooner than in one source's shuffle, whose list is
+made anew at each change. Skip stays inside the source. The soundtrack remembered for the next start stays your own choice in the screen. Offline, the logic is tested with a
+stand-in title; `BO3_HOOKREQ_ZMIX=OFF` compiles it out.
+
